.Dd July 30, 2026
.Dt NOTIFYCMP 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm notifycmp
.Nd capability-mode publish, subscribe, and timer service
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
implements
.Dq org.5bsd.notify
version 1.0.0 from
.Pa /Capabilities/System/NotifyCmp.cap .
A system-scoped router owns the topic index, bounded client queues, and
monotonic
.Xr kqueue 2
timers.
Each global service connection receives a separate relay worker that enters
capability mode.
The provider and router remain in their own coalition, so one consumer exit
cannot
terminate notification delivery for other services.
.Pp
Subscriptions are exact topic matches.
Publisher identity comes from the authenticated component bootstrap and
cannot be supplied by the publisher.
Queues, topic count, timer count, topic length, and payload size are bounded.
A full subscriber queue drops the newest event for that subscriber and
increments its drop counter without blocking unrelated subscribers.
Queues are volatile.
A publish reply confirms router processing and loss accounting, not durable
subscriber delivery; events are not replayed after restart.
.Sh SECURITY
The router receives session endpoints only from the provider factory.
Consumer channels and router endpoints are non-transferable and locked
against fork and exec propagation.
Relays cannot create sockets, fork, exec, receive descriptors, or use ambient
filesystem authority.
Subscription, publication, timer, bootstrap, and rejection decisions are
available through OpenBSM audit records and DTrace probes.
.Pp
Each session is deny-by-default.
Until an authenticated identity-bound ACL source is implemented, publication,
subscription, and timers are denied.
The relay enforces these grants before forwarding a request to the shared
router.
Subscribers should also validate the authenticated publisher identity carried
in each event when that identity is relevant to application policy.
.Sh SEE ALSO
